<title>USA: Cisco's Granite deal called strategic.</title>
<headline>Cisco's Granite deal called strategic.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cisco Systems Inc' deal to acquire Granite Systems Inc for $220 million gives it a foothold in yet another cutting-edge technology and bolsters its leadership in the networking market, analysts said.</p>
<p>Granite is a start-up with no appreciable sales but it is a pioneer in very fast, or gigabit, data packet switching.</p>
<p>&quot;People might think it is mindboggling to pay $220 million for a company with no revenues and that's not shipping product, but this is so strategic and so significant...that it positions them appreciably better,&quot; said Noel Lindsay of DMG Technology Group.</p>
</text>
